WEBVTT

00:00:02.170 --> 00:00:04.640
The three separated at a fork in the road.

00:00:05.220 --> 00:00:08.150
And now their whereabouts are undisclosed. Do they want to protect themselves? Other people?

00:00:08.150 --> 00:00:09.860
Or heavenly dreams?

00:00:10.520 --> 00:00:12.820
The creases of disorder are a cauldron of three.

00:00:13.560 --> 00:00:15.450
To an endless, eternal picture of Hell,

00:00:16.350 --> 00:00:19.530
pushing through time a door is dispelled.

00:00:20.190 --> 00:00:24.860
Your grudge shall be released.

00:00:37.640 --> 00:00:40.010
“The Midnight Silence”!

00:00:40.010 --> 00:00:42.530
This is DJ Joutarou!

00:00:42.530 --> 00:00:44.560
And, what’s the next news?

00:00:44.560 --> 00:00:47.310
Oh, a regular customer! As always, thank you.

00:00:47.310 --> 00:00:49.660
Saigawara city’s Chi-chan.

00:00:49.660 --> 00:00:52.660
Hmm? Looks like a request for a new corner.

00:00:52.660 --> 00:00:56.630
Let me see… The title is “Time for Hell Correspondence”?

00:00:57.670 --> 00:01:04.160
A corner where you let everyone hear what annoys you, or angers you, and then ferry your bad feelings to Hell?

00:01:04.670 --> 00:01:06.790
But using outdated slang now?{But using ”gyafun” now?!

00:01:20.570 --> 00:01:22.360
They read mine again!

00:01:22.980 --> 00:01:25.330
You’re always so interesting, Chi-chan!

00:01:25.330 --> 00:01:29.210
Well, yet again, I’ll give you the novelty of the show, a bell bracelet!

00:01:29.210 --> 00:01:31.200
Yes! This makes five!

00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:32.920
Well then, again tomorrow!

00:01:33.300 --> 00:01:35.190
If you want to hear the next part, attend my dreams.

00:01:35.800 --> 00:01:37.370
This was Shijima Joutarou.

00:01:37.370 --> 00:01:38.350
Bye~!

00:01:38.350 --> 00:01:39.950
Good night, Joutarou.

00:03:19.370 --> 00:03:24.970
This program is made possible by Sony Music, Aniplex,

00:03:25.390 --> 00:03:28.970
and the listed sponsors.

00:03:36.870 --> 00:03:38.550
Hey, hey, did you hear yesterday?

00:03:38.550 --> 00:03:39.950
I did!

00:03:39.950 --> 00:03:41.090
That’s…

00:03:43.590 --> 00:03:46.150
Um, Hamano-san?

00:03:46.960 --> 00:03:49.010
Sorry if we’re mistaken.

00:03:49.380 --> 00:03:53.470
Hamano-san, did you write that postcard which was signed Chi-chan?

00:03:53.470 --> 00:03:54.980
What?

00:03:54.980 --> 00:03:56.490
I thought so!

00:03:56.490 --> 00:03:58.210
Saigawara city’s Chi-chan?

00:03:59.270 --> 00:04:01.780
What? No! Really?

00:04:01.780 --> 00:04:03.080
Chi-chan?

00:04:03.480 --> 00:04:05.420
Amazing! Amazing!

00:04:05.420 --> 00:04:06.310
Um…

00:04:06.310 --> 00:04:07.510
Wow!

00:04:07.510 --> 00:04:10.440
Your mail was used yesterday too, right?

00:04:10.440 --> 00:04:11.220
What, what?

00:04:11.220 --> 00:04:12.490
What’s up with Hamano-san?

00:04:15.440 --> 00:04:18.660
Hamano-san’s mail was used on the radio!

00:04:18.660 --> 00:04:19.660
What?

00:04:19.660 --> 00:04:21.000
Not really…

00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:23.020
Amazing!

00:04:23.020 --> 00:04:23.670
What?

00:04:23.670 --> 00:04:25.150
What radio show is it?

00:04:25.150 --> 00:04:26.000
Well…

00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:30.020
Shijima Joutarou’s “The Midnight Silence”!

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:32.020
Is it a well-known show?

00:04:32.020 --> 00:04:33.430
Well…

00:04:33.430 --> 00:04:38.210
Of course! People say it’s revolutionary within the world of radio!

00:04:38.210 --> 00:04:39.590
What? Really?

00:04:40.120 --> 00:04:42.000
I’ll listen to that show!

00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:43.020
Me too!

00:04:43.230 --> 00:04:46.710
Well, let’s all listen to it from today on!

00:04:46.710 --> 00:04:50.020
When it comes to this, this whole class has Shiji-mania!

00:04:50.020 --> 00:04:52.530
What’s Shiji-mania?

00:04:52.530 --> 00:04:57.520
Shijima Joutaro and “The Midnight Silence” mania! Abbreviate, Shiji-mania!

00:04:59.570 --> 00:05:00.430
…You know.

00:05:01.430 --> 00:05:04.030
Nice, Chi-chan! That was cool!

00:05:04.040 --> 00:05:07.540
How nice! I never knew!

00:05:14.180 --> 00:05:16.380
I was so surprised today!

00:05:16.380 --> 00:05:19.520
Good evening! This is Shijima Joutarou!

00:05:22.550 --> 00:05:25.390
I wonder if everyone’s really listening.

00:05:30.400 --> 00:05:33.690
The fact that I leaked Shiji-mania.

00:05:34.030 --> 00:05:37.200
Yeah, Joutarou, I’m a Shiji-maniac.

00:05:37.200 --> 00:05:39.040
I was kind of pleased.

00:05:39.420 --> 00:05:41.190
“The Midnight Silence”.

00:05:41.190 --> 00:05:45.410
Tonight, within “The Midnight Silence”, I’ll slip into your ears.

00:05:45.790 --> 00:05:48.670
I just love Joutarou’s voice!

00:05:49.330 --> 00:05:51.750
The one who thought of the opening greeting was…

00:05:51.750 --> 00:05:53.600
Radio-name, Frog Princess!

00:05:54.190 --> 00:05:56.500
This person’s read a lot, too.

00:05:56.500 --> 00:05:57.940
Frog Princess, eh?

00:06:01.280 --> 00:06:03.430
Well then, those that have worries and also can’t sleep,

00:06:03.430 --> 00:06:05.920
spend a little time with me!

00:06:06.430 --> 00:06:08.860
Well then, the next corner!

00:06:08.860 --> 00:06:10.430
No, no!

00:06:12.180 --> 00:06:13.950
What? I’m wrong?

00:06:15.000 --> 00:06:16.060
This corn-?

00:06:18.170 --> 00:06:19.720
Uh- Sorry, sorry.

00:06:19.720 --> 00:06:22.470
The scenario writer, Yume-san, interrupted me.

00:06:23.180 --> 00:06:24.460
Then…

00:06:24.460 --> 00:06:26.550
I said that mail comes first!

00:06:27.210 --> 00:06:29.180
Yes, yes, this, right?

00:06:29.750 --> 00:06:34.580
Well, this is DJ Shijima Joutarou, 25, who still can’t listen to the writer.

00:06:37.440 --> 00:06:40.550
Joutarou’s being scolded by Yume-san yet again.

00:06:43.220 --> 00:06:45.560
Hey, didn’t something good happen to you today?

00:06:46.380 --> 00:06:48.000
I put a spell on you.

00:06:48.580 --> 00:06:51.690
More than yesterday, today; more than today, tomorrow.

00:06:52.090 --> 00:06:56.680
Like how the moon waxes, the spell changes a little bit daily.

00:06:57.070 --> 00:07:01.830
All girls are main characters; they can become Cinderella at any time.

00:07:02.570 --> 00:07:06.680
Tonight’s a full moon. Let’s count to three and look at the sky together.

00:07:11.770 --> 00:07:13.330
Joutarou…

00:07:14.120 --> 00:07:16.390
So, are you ready?

00:07:16.390 --> 00:07:17.610
Let’s go.

00:07:17.610 --> 00:07:18.750
Three…

00:07:18.750 --> 00:07:19.870
Two…

00:07:19.870 --> 00:07:20.860
One…

00:07:28.140 --> 00:07:29.270
It’s beautiful!

00:07:32.950 --> 00:07:35.860
It’s beautiful, Joutarou!

00:07:41.570 --> 00:07:43.610
Cinderella, eh?

00:07:44.060 --> 00:07:45.630
Finally, an announcement!

00:07:45.630 --> 00:07:49.150
The new corner, requested by Chi-chan, will be created!

00:07:49.150 --> 00:07:51.170
That which happens around you and annoys you,

00:07:51.170 --> 00:07:54.590
that which has been making you go crazy, but could never be told.

00:07:54.590 --> 00:07:59.090
Those bad feelings you want to ferry to Hell, send them all to me!

00:07:59.090 --> 00:08:01.850
What is this frivolous manner of speech?

00:08:02.260 --> 00:08:04.670
Amongst the young girls, he’s hugely popular,

00:08:04.670 --> 00:08:05.840
DJ Joutarou.

00:08:06.370 --> 00:08:09.840
Are girls nowadays into this kind of fluffy guy?

00:08:09.850 --> 00:08:11.590
Well then, again tomorrow!

00:08:12.080 --> 00:08:14.350
If you want to hear the next part, attend my dreams.

00:08:14.770 --> 00:08:15.860
What?

00:08:15.860 --> 00:08:17.690
This was Shijima Joutarou!

00:08:18.200 --> 00:08:19.380
Bye~!

00:08:22.590 --> 00:08:24.260
Waro-waro, have you finished writing?

00:08:25.010 --> 00:08:28.350
What are you going to do, writing all these postcards, hime?

00:08:28.350 --> 00:08:30.910
I’m going to contribute a lot more than before!

00:08:31.450 --> 00:08:35.830
There are already thirty cards! How many more times do I have to write the same thing?

00:08:36.210 --> 00:08:37.630
One hundred more!

00:08:37.630 --> 00:08:38.840
What?!

00:08:41.840 --> 00:08:43.900
Chi-chan, you’re amazing!

00:08:43.900 --> 00:08:46.830
The new corner you thought of is starting!

00:08:46.840 --> 00:08:49.910
This is proof you were recognized by Joutarou!

00:08:49.910 --> 00:08:50.890
It can’t be…

00:08:50.890 --> 00:08:52.600
Yuzuki, you were listening too, right?

00:08:53.050 --> 00:08:54.080
Yeah.

00:08:54.080 --> 00:08:57.310
Even though I was a bit surprised by the contents of the corner.

00:08:56.450 --> 00:08:59.320
See? I’ll tell you all about it!

00:09:19.070 --> 00:09:20.550
Hamano-senpai!

00:09:20.550 --> 00:09:21.420
Me?

00:09:22.110 --> 00:09:25.450
Senpai, can we see your bell bracelet?

00:09:25.800 --> 00:09:27.350
What? This?

00:09:28.610 --> 00:09:32.310
Hamano-senpai, would you join the broadcasting club, even though it’s late?

00:09:34.270 --> 00:09:36.810
What? That’s a bit…

00:09:37.230 --> 00:09:40.650
If you join, Hamano-senpai, everyone will be so happy!

00:09:41.140 --> 00:09:43.320
Please, Hamano-senpai!

00:09:43.470 --> 00:09:45.350
Well…

00:09:45.840 --> 00:09:48.820
I’ll think about it!

00:09:51.330 --> 00:09:53.100
Well then, excuse me.

00:09:53.960 --> 00:09:57.830
By the way, Hamano, I heard your mail was read on the radio.

00:09:58.200 --> 00:09:59.860
The Midnight something?

00:09:59.860 --> 00:10:00.840
Well, um…

00:10:00.840 --> 00:10:04.670
I contributed a lot during middle school, too…

00:10:05.270 --> 00:10:07.340
But my letters were never read on air.

00:10:07.340 --> 00:10:08.680
I see…

00:10:09.060 --> 00:10:10.830
Looks like you have some talent!

00:10:12.440 --> 00:10:14.670
Keep it up! Good luck!

00:10:21.890 --> 00:10:22.760
Chi-chan!

00:10:24.690 --> 00:10:26.270
Bye-bye, Chi-chan!

00:10:26.700 --> 00:10:29.400
We’ll listen to the radio again today for sure!

00:10:30.990 --> 00:10:34.330
Is this Cinderella’s Magic?

00:10:39.500 --> 00:10:43.290
Cinderella’s Magic… Cinderella’s Magic!

00:10:43.800 --> 00:10:46.110
Um… Hamano Chiriko-chan?

00:10:46.110 --> 00:10:47.050
That’s me!

00:10:50.550 --> 00:10:51.620
What?

00:10:52.850 --> 00:10:56.100
I’m called Shimura Kaname from B-class.

00:10:56.100 --> 00:10:57.030
Oh…

00:10:57.030 --> 00:10:58.880
Um… I want to listen to the radio…

00:10:58.890 --> 00:11:01.960
Oh, you should listen sometime, too!

00:11:01.960 --> 00:11:03.510
“The Midnight Silence”!

00:11:03.510 --> 00:11:04.900
It will be interesting, for sure!

00:11:04.900 --> 00:11:06.890
Yes, I know.

00:11:09.040 --> 00:11:11.910
I’m Frog Princess.

00:11:11.910 --> 00:11:15.180
Really? You’re that Frog Princess?

00:11:15.180 --> 00:11:17.390
What? Really?

00:11:18.930 --> 00:11:20.670
Amazing! Did you hear yesterday?

00:11:20.670 --> 00:11:21.920
Yes, I did!

00:11:21.920 --> 00:11:23.190
You were being used, weren’t you?

00:11:23.190 --> 00:11:24.310
Yeah!

00:11:38.740 --> 00:11:39.640
This.

00:11:40.010 --> 00:11:42.180
Wow! Just as I expected from the Frog Princess!

00:11:42.180 --> 00:11:43.960
That’s an amazing number of bell bracelets!

00:11:44.600 --> 00:11:48.650
I was always interested in what kind of girl Chi-chan was.

00:11:48.650 --> 00:11:53.910
I was interested too, since Frog Princess is always read out.

00:11:55.460 --> 00:12:00.850
I remember the first time your mail was used.

00:12:01.830 --> 00:12:05.050
“Yesterday, Joutarou appeared in my dream.”

00:12:05.050 --> 00:12:07.790
“It was a dream where we dated at an amusement park.”

00:12:08.100 --> 00:12:13.420
“Joutarou, when riding the ferris wheel, held my hand softly,” it said.

00:12:14.540 --> 00:12:18.010
In truth, that day, I saw the same dream.

00:12:18.010 --> 00:12:19.470
What?

00:12:19.880 --> 00:12:23.310
After that, I was always interested in Chi-chan.

00:12:24.730 --> 00:12:27.980
I love your mail, Chi-chan!

00:12:29.680 --> 00:12:33.260
Me too, I love Frog Princess’s mail!

00:12:34.490 --> 00:12:37.990
Really? Thank you! I’m glad!

00:13:02.890 --> 00:13:07.010
The Cinderella’s Magic Joutarou cast on me is amazing!

00:13:07.460 --> 00:13:12.540
This question has arrived: “What kind of behavior do you like in a girl?”

00:13:13.080 --> 00:13:15.450
Behavior? I guess…

00:13:17.610 --> 00:13:20.920
The type that dries her hair after getting out of the bath?

00:13:23.160 --> 00:13:25.040
Hey, Yume-san, don’t laugh at me!

00:13:25.040 --> 00:13:28.040
Oh, and for shampoo, I like the type you use in the bath.

00:13:28.810 --> 00:13:33.270
Even so, girls always have a sweet odor like candy.

00:13:36.260 --> 00:13:38.920
A sweet odor?

00:13:41.060 --> 00:13:44.050
What was that sweet talk?

00:13:44.700 --> 00:13:48.150
It’s a basic skill used to capture the hearts of girls.

00:13:48.790 --> 00:13:52.090
All show and no heart, it seems.

00:13:53.040 --> 00:13:56.330
Next is a message from radio name Kikuri-san!

00:13:56.330 --> 00:13:59.630
Yes! I’m being used before Ai!

00:14:08.330 --> 00:14:10.040
It really happened?

00:14:10.040 --> 00:14:12.510
Yeah, I was so excited!

00:14:14.770 --> 00:14:18.010
Why am I always not used in times like this?

00:14:18.350 --> 00:14:20.580
A lifelong failure!

00:14:20.580 --> 00:14:22.140
Are you tired from exam studies?

00:14:23.060 --> 00:14:23.950
Maybe…

00:14:26.460 --> 00:14:29.160
And, since I couldn’t fall asleep,

00:14:29.160 --> 00:14:33.350
I thought about why I like Joutarou’s talk so much.

00:14:34.480 --> 00:14:39.060
It’s like there aren’t any lies in his words.

00:14:40.360 --> 00:14:45.680
Since he picks words himself, and tells us by himself.

00:14:45.680 --> 00:14:49.020
Maybe that’s why it resonates in our hearts so well!

00:14:49.710 --> 00:14:50.520
Sure.

00:14:51.530 --> 00:14:54.690
I want to say thank you to Joutarou!

00:14:55.540 --> 00:14:58.430
“Thank you for meeting me.

00:14:58.430 --> 00:15:02.090
Thank you for casting Cinderella’s Magic on me!” like that.

00:15:04.220 --> 00:15:05.540
Hey, Chi-chan.

00:15:06.630 --> 00:15:09.110
Do you want to go meet Joutarou together?

00:15:19.110 --> 00:15:23.010
K-Kaname-chan! I’m getting nervous!

00:15:23.330 --> 00:15:26.230
It’s impossible! Waiting for his arrival!

00:15:26.230 --> 00:15:28.290
Come on, Chi-chan, pull it together!

00:15:28.290 --> 00:15:30.950
You’re going to thank Joutarou, right?

00:15:30.950 --> 00:15:31.620
But!

00:15:43.060 --> 00:15:44.350
Kiuchi Yume-san!

00:15:44.820 --> 00:15:45.640
Uh…

00:15:45.640 --> 00:15:46.850
Um…

00:15:46.850 --> 00:15:52.650
Our mail was read on “The Midnight Silence”, and-!

00:15:52.650 --> 00:15:55.650
Oh, are you waiting for Joutarou to come?

00:15:55.650 --> 00:15:56.650
Yes!

00:15:56.650 --> 00:15:59.010
Oh, sure! I got it!

00:15:59.010 --> 00:16:02.650
Fans waiting for him means Joutarou’s gotten quite famous!

00:16:03.090 --> 00:16:05.150
Um… Yume-san!

00:16:06.660 --> 00:16:07.890
I…

00:16:08.280 --> 00:16:12.170
I want to become a radio scenario writer!

00:16:12.170 --> 00:16:12.950
What?

00:16:13.320 --> 00:16:15.900
Yume-san’s my idol!

00:16:15.900 --> 00:16:19.660
I want to someday become a writer like you!

00:16:21.330 --> 00:16:22.410
I see.

00:16:23.250 --> 00:16:27.180
Hey, what kind of job do you think writing is?

00:16:27.180 --> 00:16:29.760
Um… That…

00:16:31.220 --> 00:16:32.690
Of course you have no idea.

00:16:32.690 --> 00:16:35.950
I was like you at your age.

00:16:35.950 --> 00:16:39.660
Not knowing about anything concrete,

00:16:39.660 --> 00:16:43.060
I just knew vaguely I wanted to become a writer.

00:16:43.060 --> 00:16:44.700
Yume-san, too?

00:16:44.700 --> 00:16:47.740
Oh right, I’ll give you this.

00:16:48.900 --> 00:16:50.860
One step into the future.

00:16:52.070 --> 00:16:53.810
It’s a script I wrote.

00:16:54.280 --> 00:16:55.880
First, you must know.

00:16:57.620 --> 00:17:00.170
Wow! I’m so happy! Thank you very much!

00:17:01.930 --> 00:17:03.060
A script?

00:17:03.420 --> 00:17:09.230
“Girls’ behavior? I guess… The type that dries her hair after getting out of the bath.”

00:17:09.230 --> 00:17:11.890
That’s the same as what Joutarou said yesterday…

00:17:12.310 --> 00:17:14.890
Yes, that’s the job of the writer.

00:17:16.960 --> 00:17:18.690
Is this the first time you’ve seen a script?

00:17:18.690 --> 00:17:22.030
Yes! So this is what a script is like!

00:17:22.780 --> 00:17:25.360
But can I really have it?

00:17:25.360 --> 00:17:26.650
What? Sure.

00:17:26.650 --> 00:17:28.870
Um… What does this mean?

00:17:29.280 --> 00:17:31.790
What? What does it mean?

00:17:31.790 --> 00:17:35.790
Why is what Joutarou said written here?

00:17:35.790 --> 00:17:37.750
Oh! Well,

00:17:37.750 --> 00:17:41.300
“The Midnight Silence” is completely scripted.

00:17:41.670 --> 00:17:44.130
Completely… scripted?

00:17:52.470 --> 00:17:57.350
I write out all words and pauses in the DJ’s lines.

00:17:57.350 --> 00:18:00.810
It’s tough because you have to create a character named Shijima Joutaro.

00:18:01.230 --> 00:18:05.320
But as a writer, it’s a show worth doing.

00:18:08.460 --> 00:18:12.060
Since I thought your eyes were serious, today is special.

00:18:12.730 --> 00:18:15.120
It’ll be nice if we could write a show together sometime!

00:18:16.650 --> 00:18:18.150
Thank you very much!

00:18:18.150 --> 00:18:20.570
I’ll become a scenario writer for sure!

00:18:21.000 --> 00:18:23.010
Well then, see you later!

00:18:29.460 --> 00:18:33.190
Wow, amazing! I’m about to fall over!

00:18:43.790 --> 00:18:45.580
Completely scripted…

00:18:48.820 --> 00:18:51.820
Well then, let’s say it together!

00:18:51.820 --> 00:18:55.830
Oh, here it is again! From the Frog Princess.

00:18:56.340 --> 00:18:58.780
Let’s see… “Today something amazing happened to me”!

00:19:01.430 --> 00:19:02.950
Well then, again tomorrow!

00:19:02.950 --> 00:19:05.570
If you want to hear the next part, attend my dreams.

00:19:05.570 --> 00:19:07.170
This was Shijima Joutarou!

00:19:07.170 --> 00:19:08.240
Bye~!

00:19:19.560 --> 00:19:20.850
Chi-chan?

00:19:22.550 --> 00:19:23.560
Hone-onna.

00:19:23.560 --> 00:19:25.140
Sure, Ojou.

00:19:28.610 --> 00:19:30.070
Take this.

00:19:39.180 --> 00:19:42.800
If you really want to release your hatred,

00:19:42.800 --> 00:19:45.170
just pull that red string.

00:19:45.580 --> 00:19:51.070
If you do, it will signify signing a contract formally with me.

00:19:51.070 --> 00:19:54.760
The one you hate will swiftly be ferried to Hell.

00:19:55.870 --> 00:20:01.190
But, if you release your hatred, you must pay the price.

00:20:01.680 --> 00:20:05.780
Curse someone, and two holes are created.

00:20:05.780 --> 00:20:08.440
If you agree to the contract, your soul will also fall to Hell.

00:20:08.440 --> 00:20:09.550
Hell?

00:20:09.550 --> 00:20:11.840
Although that’s after you die.

00:20:13.000 --> 00:20:16.750
Unable to go to heaven,

00:20:16.750 --> 00:20:21.500
your soul will wander endlessly, tasting pain and suffering.

00:20:22.020 --> 00:20:25.340
The rest is up to you.

00:20:29.110 --> 00:20:32.210
Good morning! Morning! Good morning!

00:20:32.210 --> 00:20:35.030
What? What did you forget?

00:20:36.800 --> 00:20:39.750
Did you hear? Yesterday’s “The Midnight Silence”!

00:20:40.090 --> 00:20:41.130
Yeah.

00:20:41.670 --> 00:20:45.590
Thanks to Yume-san’s complete scripting, wasn’t it interesting?

00:20:47.050 --> 00:20:50.180
“The Midnight Silence” is Joutarou’s show.

00:20:51.380 --> 00:20:55.620
Sure, but isn’t its popularity down to Yume-san?

00:20:56.050 --> 00:21:00.710
Really, wasn’t Joutarou lucky to find such an amazing writer?

00:21:03.030 --> 00:21:04.430
Joutarou…

00:21:04.960 --> 00:21:09.510
Today I’m excited in a different way than yesterday!

00:21:09.510 --> 00:21:10.510
Right?

00:21:12.330 --> 00:21:13.970
What’s up, Chi-chan?

00:21:14.770 --> 00:21:19.470
Kaname-chan, the complete scripting, have you told anybody?

00:21:19.470 --> 00:21:21.980
No, not at all.

00:21:22.880 --> 00:21:23.760
Oh.

00:21:26.490 --> 00:21:27.480
I’m glad.

00:21:28.980 --> 00:21:29.970
What?

00:21:32.490 --> 00:21:35.260
Your hatred is received.

00:21:58.260 --> 00:21:58.820
What?

00:21:58.820 --> 00:21:59.550
What is this?

00:22:01.030 --> 00:22:05.100
This grudge will ferry you to Hell.

00:22:14.820 --> 00:22:18.000
The one who thought of tonight’s opening greeting was…

00:22:18.000 --> 00:22:23.280
Let’s see… Oh, usage level is high! Chi-chan!

00:22:23.650 --> 00:22:25.050
Thank you, as always!

00:22:25.050 --> 00:22:27.120
So, first, we’ve kept you waiting for this new corner!

00:22:27.120 --> 00:22:30.000
“Time for Hell Correspondence”!

00:22:44.880 --> 00:22:49.970
I shall release your hatred.

00:22:44.960 --> 00:22:49.970
Note: Candle says Hamano Chiriko.

00:24:20.850 --> 00:24:21.660
Your name?

00:24:22.160 --> 00:24:23.490
Nakiri Kaori.

00:24:23.700 --> 00:24:25.650
You’re a heiress for flower arrangement?

00:24:26.010 --> 00:24:30.150
Being born with my life set out in front of me- I couldn’t stand it.

00:24:31.160 --> 00:24:33.180
So I ran away from home, and lived alone.

00:24:34.660 --> 00:24:36.910
But I found out accidentally!

00:24:37.420 --> 00:24:41.330
The instinct flows through me, and I can’t wash it away.

00:24:42.420 --> 00:24:44.430
Fate, eh?

00:24:45.440 --> 00:24:48.610
Next time: Snow, Moon, Flowers.

00:24:50.710 --> 00:24:55.880
This program is made possible by Sony Music, Aniplex,

00:24:55.880 --> 00:24:58.990
and the listed sponsors.
